<?xml version='1.0' encoding='UTF-8'?>
<TcPlcObject Version="1.1.0.1">
  <POU Name="FB_AnalogInput16" Id="{4e536554-b217-4cb4-b0ce-72d63127ea2f}" SpecialFunc="None">
    <Declaration><![CDATA[
(*
    FB_AnalogInput16 - analog input channel of a 16-bit terminal (EL31xx)

    Converts the signed 16-bit raw value of one terminal channel into
    engineering units, provides a moving average, and reports the terminal's
    status bits as errors.

    I/O (link in the I/O configuration):
        Raw            AT %I*  INT    channel value
        TerminalError  AT %I*  BOOL   optional, channel status bit "Error"
        Overrange      AT %I*  BOOL   optional, channel status bit "Overrange"
        Underrange     AT %I*  BOOL   optional, channel status bit "Underrange"
    Unlinked status bits stay FALSE and never cause an error.

    Use from ST:
        // once, e.g. in the initialization part of MAIN
        Ai1.SetScalePreset(Preset := MBIDivB.E_AiScalePreset.EL31XX_LEGACY, NominalFullScale := 10.0);
        // or a manual pair:
        // Ai1.SetScale(RawFullScale := 32767, ValueFullScale := 10.0);

        // every cycle
        Ai1();
        Acq.Channel[1].Input := Ai1.Status.Value;

    Scaling until SetScale/SetScalePreset is called: EL31XX_LEGACY, 10.0.

    Methods (ST only):
        SetScalePreset(Preset : E_AiScalePreset; NominalFullScale : REAL) : BOOL
        SetScale(RawFullScale : DINT; ValueFullScale : REAL) : BOOL
            Status.Value = Raw x ValueFullScale / RawFullScale. A RawFullScale
            of 0 is rejected with an error, and the previous scaling stays.
            Returns TRUE if accepted. An accepted call clears that error.

    Cfg (written by the client):
        FilterSize      DINT        live; number of values averaged into
                                    ValueFiltered, limited to
                                    1..GVL_Param.AI_FILTER_MAX_LENGTH (values
                                    outside are written back clamped); a
                                    change restarts the average; default 50

    Status (read only):
        State           INT         always 0
        StateText       STRING(20)  always 'ACTIVE'
        Error           BOOL        TRUE while a linked status bit is set, or
                                    after a rejected SetScale/SetScalePreset
        ErrorText       STRING(80)  'Terminal reports error' / 'overrange' /
                                    'underrange', or the rejected call
        Value           REAL        engineering units (e.g. V), scaled raw value
        ValueFiltered   REAL        engineering units, mean of the last
                                    FilterSize values (of all values while
                                    fewer have been received since a restart)
        Raw             DINT        last raw value
        RawFullScale    DINT        raw value of the active scaling ...
        ValueFullScale  REAL        ... and its engineering value

    Memory: GVL_Param.AI_FILTER_MAX_LENGTH x 4 B (4 KiB with the default).
*)
FUNCTION_BLOCK FB_AnalogInput16 EXTENDS FB_AnalogInputBase
VAR_INPUT
    Raw AT %I* : INT;
    TerminalError AT %I* : BOOL;
    Overrange AT %I* : BOOL;
    Underrange AT %I* : BOOL;
END_VAR
]]></Declaration>
    <Implementation>
      <ST><![CDATA[
Update(Raw := INT_TO_DINT(Raw), TerminalError := TerminalError, Overrange := Overrange, Underrange := Underrange);
]]></ST>
    </Implementation>
  </POU>
</TcPlcObject>